>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 366 0 R
/T (Dynamic Resource Mapping: Instead of hard-coded structures, the system uses a Configuration Parser to build a network of named buffers and threads at runtime. This allows for the flexible definition of buffer capacities and thread roles \(Producer, Consumer, or Pipeline Worker\) via external config files.)
/E (Dynamic Resource Mapping: Instead of hard-coded structures, the system uses a Configuration Parser to build a network of named buffers and threads at runtime. This allows for the flexible definition of buffer capacities and thread roles \(Producer, Consumer, or Pipeline Worker\) via external config files.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 367 0 R
/T (Thread Context Abstraction: Every thread is decoupled from the main logic using a Thread Context structure. This structure encapsulates all operational data, such as timing intervals and buffer references, allowing the same generic code to handle diverse tasks depending on its assigned context.)
/E (Thread Context Abstraction: Every thread is decoupled from the main logic using a Thread Context structure. This structure encapsulates all operational data, such as timing intervals and buffer references, allowing the same generic code to handle diverse tasks depending on its assigned context.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 368 0 R
/T (Decentralized Synchronization: To maximize concurrency, each named buffer operates as an independent synchronization unit. By utilizing localized POSIX Mutexes and Condition Variables \(not_full, not_empty\), the design ensures that threads only block when their specific resource is unavailable, preventing global system bottlenecks.)
/E (Decentralized Synchronization: To maximize concurrency, each named buffer operates as an independent synchronization unit. By utilizing localized POSIX Mutexes and Condition Variables \(not_full, not_empty\), the design ensures that threads only block when their specific resource is unavailable, preventing global system bottlenecks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 369 0 R
/T (Active Graph-Based Monitoring: The system incorporates a dedicated Deadlock Monitor that maintains a real-time state of the simulation. By tracking "held" and "requested" resources for every thread, it constructs a Wait-for Graph to proactively detect circular dependencies.)
/E (Active Graph-Based Monitoring: The system incorporates a dedicated Deadlock Monitor that maintains a real-time state of the simulation. By tracking "held" and "requested" resources for every thread, it constructs a Wait-for Graph to proactively detect circular dependencies.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 370 0 R
/T (Graceful Termination: Reliability is ensured through a controlled shutdown protocol. Upon reaching the runtime limit, a global broadcast signal forces all sleeping threads to wake up and exit cleanly, ensuring all allocated resources are released.)
/E (Graceful Termination: Reliability is ensured through a controlled shutdown protocol. Upon reaching the runtime limit, a global broadcast signal forces all sleeping threads to wake up and exit cleanly, ensuring all allocated resources are released.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
