605 0 obj
<<
/Title (Decentralized Synchronization: To maximize concurrency, each named buffer operates as an independent synchronization unit. By utilizing localized POSIX Mutexes and Condition Variables \(not_full, not_empty\), the design ensures that threads only block when their specific resource is unavailable, preventing global system bottlenecks.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 601 0 R
/Next 609 0 R
>>
endobj
606 0 obj
<<
/Title (Graceful Termination: Reliability is ensured through a controlled shutdown protocol. Upon reaching the runtime limit, a global broadcast signal forces all sleeping threads to wake up and exit cleanly, ensuring all allocated resources are released.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 609 0 R
/Next 602 0 R
>>
endobj
